---
// The site's mark: an opening quotation mark, „ — because every word on this
// site is quoted from a 1918 newspaper, and the mark sits before the name as
// if the name itself were a quotation. Drawn as two slabs rather than set as
// a character: the page loads no web font, and a glyph would be at the mercy
// of whichever face the phone happens to use (the macrons already taught us
// that). Same two shapes as public/favicon.svg — change one, change both.
---
<svg class="mark" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <path d="M4.4 3.2H8L5.2 12.8H1.6z" /><path d="M11.2 3.2h3.6L12 12.8H8.4z" />
</svg>
